WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.391
Roxy flew after the van.

2
00:00:04.392 --> 00:00:07.235
Suddenly a bus came around a corner.

3
00:00:07.236 --> 00:00:10.253
The van made a sharp turn to avoid it.

4
00:00:10.254 --> 00:00:14.215
The van hit a traffic light and knocked it over.

5
00:00:14.216 --> 00:00:16.734
"Ahh!" a man cried.

6
00:00:16.735 --> 00:00:19.510
Roxy caught the traffic light.

7
00:00:19.511 --> 00:00:25.153
"Thanks, Rocket Girl!" the man said.

8
00:00:25.154 --> 00:00:28.159
Roxy found the van.

9
00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.773
She followed it into the mountains.

10
00:00:30.774 --> 00:00:35.666
"Maybe the driver will lead me to the other dancers."

11
00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:38.483
The van stopped near a flat rock wall.

12
00:00:38.484 --> 00:00:41.433
A hidden door in the rock slid open.

13
00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:47.425
The van drove in. Roxy shot in after it.

14
00:00:47.426 --> 00:00:52.457
The driver went into a room.

15
00:00:52.458 --> 00:00:56.082
Roxy used her x-ray vision to see through the door.

16
00:00:56.083 --> 00:00:58.739
The two missing dancers were tied up in a corner.

17
00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:02.396
Another woman was staring at a movie poster.

18
00:01:02.397 --> 00:01:06.187
"I've seen them in TV commercials," Roxy thought.

19
00:01:06.188 --> 00:01:09.045
"They're terrible actors!"

20
00:01:09.046 --> 00:01:12.386
"I'm back, Cleo," the man said.

21
00:01:12.387 --> 00:01:16.966
"Lester!" Cleo said. "Where's Harry?"

22
00:01:16.967 --> 00:01:20.031
"Eating bananas," Lester said.

23
00:01:20.032 --> 00:01:24.280
"Did he finally capture Rocket Girl?" Cleo asked.

24
00:01:24.281 --> 00:01:30.024
"Nope," Lester said. "He thinks all the Rocket Dancers are Rocket Girl."

25
00:01:30.025 --> 00:01:34.180
Cleo stomped her foot. "We weren't famous as actors.

26
00:01:34.181 --> 00:01:38.002
So you said Harry could help us become famous as villains.

27
00:01:38.003 --> 00:01:41.679
And we paid a lot of money to rent him!"

28
00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:45.621
Lester shrugged. "He's good at kidnapping people in the movies."

29
00:01:45.622 --> 00:01:52.949
"Well, we need to fire him," Cleo said, "and kidnap Rocket Girl ourselves."

30
00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:55.765
Just then Roxy fired her eye laser beams.

31
00:01:55.766 --> 00:02:01.786
Whiz-hoo! The door exploded. The villains gasped.

32
00:02:01.787 --> 00:02:05.015
"You're under arrest!" Roxy said.

33
00:02:05.016 --> 00:02:08.264
"No way!" Cleo pressed a button.

34
00:02:08.265 --> 00:02:10.907
A metal cage dropped from above.

35
00:02:10.908 --> 00:02:14.602
Clang! Bars surrounded Roxy!

36
00:02:14.603 --> 00:02:19.406
Lester grinned. "We caught Rocket Girl!"

37
00:02:19.407 --> 00:02:23.914
Cleo pumped her fist. "We're the best villains ever!"

38
00:02:23.915 --> 00:02:29.589
Roxy grabbed the bars. "Grr!" They wouldn't bend.

39
00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:31.816
She fired her eye laser beams.

40
00:02:31.817 --> 00:02:34.324
But they just bounced off the bars.

41
00:02:34.325 --> 00:02:38.233
"That is super strong steel," Lester said.

42
00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:41.961
"You'll never escape!" Cleo said.

43
00:02:41.962 --> 00:02:47.703
"Oh yeah?" Roxy spun around—faster and faster.

44
00:02:47.704 --> 00:02:50.596
She drilled into the floor and disappeared.

45
00:02:50.597 --> 00:02:55.887
Lester gulped.

46
00:02:55.888 --> 00:03:02.780
Cleo and Lester jumped into the van and sped down the road.

47
00:03:02.781 --> 00:03:06.030
Ka-boom! The road exploded in front of them.

48
00:03:06.031 --> 00:03:10.689
Roxy shot out and grabbed the van.

49
00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:15.508
She brought it to jail.

50
00:03:15.509 --> 00:03:21.091
Then she returned the missing dancers to Metro City Music Hall.

51
00:03:21.092 --> 00:03:24.220
"Thank you, Rocket Girl!" one dancer said.

52
00:03:24.221 --> 00:03:29.628
Another dancer smiled. "Thanks to you, our show won't be canceled."

53
00:03:29.629 --> 00:03:35.056
"Ugh," Roxy thought. "Now I have to see the show again!"

54
00:03:35.057 --> 00:03:43.882
But she smiled politely. "No problem!"

